Theorem RL-11: same-block donor-to-recipient owner-credit transfer

  Preconditions:
    - DP-6 identifies an Owned, non-Shared, shape-compatible candidate.
    - The donor precedes the recipient in the block.
    - No intervening throw, competing birth, or alias use occurs.
    - The donor is statically Unique.

  Soundness property:
    Forall dying donor d and fresh same-type recipient r in one block:
      (P1) RL-11 freezes the transfer relation iff all four conditions hold.
      (P2) the donor's exact owner credit becomes the recipient's credit.
      (P3) the relation is evaluator-equivalent to donor cleanup plus an
           independent recipient birth.
    Reset, Reuse, allocation identity, and storage recycling are transitional
    carrier or projection details, not theorem premises.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate:
      abc_all_hold_credit_transfer -> transfer
      recipient_before_donor_no_transfer -> no transfer
      intervening_hazard_no_transfer -> no transfer
      non_unique_no_transfer -> no transfer
    Coverage gate: 4 cases. A Shared donor is rejected.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl11_same_block_reuse)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-11 freezes a same-block donor/recipient owner-credit transfer in four exhaustive condition cases without selecting a storage-reuse mechanism
